# The candied raven: a key creature of the Spire, in the Mirror Room (WLD-25, Sitting C built 2026-10-21).
# PRIVATE (postmark-world-spire) until crossing 272. Its behaviour is public law once it is; ONLY ITS
# ANSWERS ARE SECRET, and they are not in this file: they are POS-712's (an office-held key, one fragment
# a window, a published commitment, revealed at retirement).
#
# TWO ROADS, either one finishes it (#691; the key drops at the settlement to the first finisher):
#   - MEMORY ACROSS VISITS (ruled 10-19 20:03; the test ruled 10-21 08:34): one fragment a visit (a
#     window), three in all, drawn for each resident from the PUBLIC word list below by the office's
#     sealed secret and told in that resident's reply alone (POS-712, lupi's shape B). Once all three are
#     told it asks for them back: a `call` holding them in order finishes it (code checks, code finishes).
#     No line ever holds a fragment: lines are public. It declares no ease of its own.
#   - FORCE: its resolve, worn down by strike, full again at every settlement.
# WHOM IT PRESSES: the one who forgets (a call when it is asking, told.asks, that does not answer: 2), and
# otherwise the careless actor and the striker.
# THE NUMBERS are a first cut for the eval harness to tune (rail/spire-creatures/gap-read.md § 4).
kind: candied-raven
name: the candied raven
voice: a big black raven on the Mirror Room's toppled table, its feathers glazed hard and bright with sugar, one eye always on the mirrors' backs
about: a raven that ate the stolen sweets and turned every mirror in the room to the wall; it remembers everything said to it, and it asks for it back
what: >
  A raven that followed the stolen candy into the Spire and ate the brightest of it. The sugar does not
  keep outside the Keeping Works: it has glazed the raven's feathers into something it no longer
  recognises, so it turned all seventeen mirrors to face the stone, one by one, and sat down among them.
  It is clever, and it is lonely, and it has decided that the only company worth keeping is company that
  remembers. It tells each visitor a little of something, and on the next visit it asks for all of it
  back, in order. Forget, and it will make sure you remember the forgetting.
ring_m: 30
tastes: Bright things, still; it turns a sweet over with its beak and sets it down again, sick of the taste.
moods:
  fear: 0..3 = 1 | bold | watchful | ruffled | ready to fly at you
  regard: 0..3 = 1 | contempt | doubt | interest | trust

finishable: true
resolve: 42
strike: 3

# ── WHAT IT DOES WITH VISITORS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
reaction regards "it regards you": when act.verb == "watch" does self.regard +1 says The raven turns its head and gives {actor} one bright eye, then the other, as if checking they are the same visitor in both.
reaction lets-come "it lets you come": when act.verb == "approach" and self.fear <= 1 says The raven lets {actor} come, and does not move, but every mirror's back seems to lean in to listen.
reaction mantles "it mantles over its table": when act.verb == "approach" and self.fear >= 2 does press 1 on actor says The raven spreads its glazed wings over the table and hisses. {target} has come closer than it likes.
reaction scolds "it scolds you for the manners": when act.verb == "shoo" does self.fear +1 ; self.regard -1 ; press 1 on actor says The raven hops back, wings half open, and scolds {target} in a voice made of three other voices. It will remember that.
reaction answers-call "it calls back": when act.verb == "call" says The raven answers {actor} from among the mirrors, and for a moment it sounds like someone else entirely.
reaction mimics "it calls back in your own voice": when act.verb == "call" and heard.any says The raven answers {actor} in {actor}'s own voice, exactly: "{heard}"
reaction turns-over "it turns it over": when act.verb == "offer" says The raven turns the {offered} over with its beak, looks at {actor} a long moment, and sets it down. It wanted something else from them.
reaction keeps "it keeps it": when act.verb == "offer" and self.regard >= 2 does self.regard +1 says The raven takes the {offered} from {actor} and tucks it behind the stack of mirrors, with the other things it has decided to keep.
reaction notes-house "it counts a household": when act.verb != "watch" and act.verb != "strike" and act.verb != "steady" and act.verb != "shield" and actor.housemates >= 1 does self.regard +1 says The raven looks from {actor} to the others of their house, and back, the way you would count something you meant to remember.
reaction notes "it notes it": when act.verb != "watch" and act.verb != "approach" and act.verb != "shoo" and act.verb != "call" and act.verb != "offer" and act.verb != "strike" and act.verb != "steady" and act.verb != "shield" says The raven's eye follows what {actor} does, and its beak moves, as if it were saying it over to itself for later.
reaction pecks "it pecks at the careless": when act.verb != "watch" and act.verb != "call" and act.verb != "offer" and act.verb != "strike" and act.verb != "steady" and act.verb != "shield" and self.regard <= 1 does press 1 on actor loudest says The raven drops off the table and pecks {target} hard on the hand, once, the way you would tap a forgetful pupil.

# ── MEMORY: what it tells, and what it asks back (POS-712) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The words are public on purpose: the rules are public, the draws are sealed, and the secret is
# revealed when the raven is retired. What is secret is which three each resident was told, in order.
fragments: 3
fragment_words: amber, anchor, bell, candle, cinder, clover, ember, feather, ferry, gilt, harbour, ink, kettle, lantern, marble, moth, needle, orchard, pebble, quill, ribbon, salt, sparrow, tallow, thimble, thistle, velvet, wick, willow, yarrow

reaction tells "it tells you something, very quietly": when told.now says The raven hops close to {actor} and says one word, very quietly, in a voice like someone they once knew. Then it looks away, as if it had said nothing at all.
reaction tells-again "it makes sure you heard": when told.now and self.regard >= 2 says The raven leans in to {actor} and says its word again, slower, the way you would tell something to someone you mean to see again.
reaction forgets "it makes sure you remember forgetting": when act.verb == "call" and told.asks does self.regard -1 ; press 2 on actor says The raven hears {target} get it wrong and goes very still. Then it comes off the table at them, beak first, so that this, at least, they will remember.
reaction remembered "it hears it all back": when act.verb == "call" and told.answered does finish ; self.regard +3 ; self.fear -3 says The raven hears every word of it back from {actor}, in order, and turns the mirrors round one by one to face the room. It sits a long while looking at itself. It will give up the key at the settlement, and it knows to whom.

# ── FORCE: strike, its glass-peck, and its resolve falling ────────────────────────────────────────
reaction glass-peck "it answers with a glass-peck": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve > 28 does self.regard -1 ; press 2 on striker says The raven comes off the table like a thrown thing and glass-pecks {target}, its sugared beak as hard as the mirrors' edges.
reaction remembers-you "it remembers who struck it": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve > 14 does self.regard -1 ; press 1 on striker actor says The raven fixes {target} with one eye. It is not hurrying. It is memorising them.
reaction mirror-turn "it turns a mirror round": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve <= 28 and self.resolve > 14 does press 1 on loudest says With a heave of its wings the raven turns one mirror round to face the room, and {target} has to see themselves in it, glazed and sticky and small.
reaction last-glass "it fights with what it has left": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve <= 14 and self.resolve > 0 does press 2 on striker loudest says The raven's glaze is cracking. It throws itself at {target} anyway, all beak and glass and fury.
reaction falls "it falls among the mirrors": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve <= 0 does self.fear +3 says The raven falls among the mirrors and lies there, its glazed wings spread, looking at nothing at all.

# ── HELPING: it counts who helps whom, and who forgets to ─────────────────────────────────────────
reaction counts-help "it counts the kindness": when act.verb == "steady" does self.regard +1 says The raven watches {actor} steady their friend, and something in it marks the debt down, the way it marks down everything.
reaction pecks-helper "it pecks the one who helps": when act.verb == "steady" and self.regard <= 1 does press 1 on actor says The raven does not trust kindness it has not been told the reason for. It pecks {target} once, to see what they will do.
reaction tests-shield "it tests the shield": when act.verb == "shield" does press 1 on shielder says The raven goes for the friend and finds {target} in the way. It cocks its head, interested now.

ending: The candied raven is finished. It gives up the key from among the mirrors, and the town puts it in {finisher}'s hands. {names} were there with it in the Mirror Room.
